{
    "background_story": "Mama was a kind-hearted, creative soul who ran a small, quirky craft shop in the town square. She was affectionately known as the 'Stamper Queen' among locals and visitors alike. Mama's passion was rubber stamping, and she spent most of her days designing and carving intricate stamps that brought joy to all who used them. Her shop was a treasure trove of colorful inks, papers, and stamps, and Mama loved nothing more than helping customers create their own unique masterpieces. As a stamper, Mama's artistry was not limited to paper; she also stamped her love and warmth into the hearts of everyone who entered her shop. Her infectious laughter and generous spirit made her a beloved fixture in the community, and her stamps continue to spread happiness far and wide.",
